                <pb facs="0576" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2516a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-10T19:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>304. A press report this afternoon from London states that the French Government
                    is preparing to invite the American Government to adhere to the proposed
                    European Pact of Non-intervention in the Spanish civil war.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph at once any information which you can obtain respecting the
                    correctness of this report. A similar telegram is being sent to London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
